  "village_rule": "each cell takes the name of the nearest OSM place=village/suburb/quarter point",
  "caveat": "Bathtub model on a 30 m DEM: no tide timing, drainage, sea walls, pumps, embankments or rainfall. Copernicus GLO-30 is a surface model (roofs, trees), so built-up ground reads high and the flood is understated. Heights are above the EGM2008 geoid, which is not local mean sea level, and the DEM dates from 2011-2015: where land is sinking (the Java north coast) today's ground is lower than it reads. Roads are dropped when any point along them is below the level, so a road crossing an unmapped culvert or ford counts as under water. Shelters are the ones OSM has.",
